<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN"
  "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for the Developer ID (outside the Mac App Store) build.

  App Sandbox is deliberately ABSENT. It is not required for Developer ID
  distribution, and it would break the run_python chat tool, which
  sandboxes each call itself with sandbox-exec and cannot be nested.

  The hardened runtime IS applied (the "runtime" codesign option, set in
  bundle-app.sh) because notarization requires it. Each opt-out below
  names something the hardened runtime would otherwise deny.

  NOTE for editors: XML forbids a double hyphen inside a comment, and
  AMFI rejects the entire file over one while plutil -lint still reports
  OK. So name flags in prose here, never verbatim.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!-- REQUIRED. The hardened runtime otherwise refuses to load any
       library not signed by the same Team ID, and vpipe dlopens two
       kinds that never will be:
         * FFmpeg from the host (Homebrew's, when it is not bundled);
           the unbundled mode is a supported configuration, not a
           fallback.
         * plugin .dylibs built by whoever wrote them (docs/PLUGINS.md).
       Bundling FFmpeg does not remove the need: plugins remain. -->
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
  <true/>

  <!-- Capture stages and live vision/audio model input. Paired with the
       NSCameraUsageDescription / NSMicrophoneUsageDescription strings in
       Info.plist; both halves are needed. -->
  <key>com.apple.security.device.camera</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
  <true/>

  <!--
    Deliberately NOT requested:

    com.apple.developer.networking.multicast
        ONVIF discovery falls back to a subnet scan when multicast is
        unavailable, so the feature works without it. Requesting it
        would add an Apple review cycle for no functional gain.

    com.apple.security.cs.allow-dyld-environment-variables
        The bundled FFmpeg is found through @loader_path, which the
        hardened runtime honours. DYLD_* would need this entitlement
        precisely because the runtime strips those variables; using
        @loader_path avoids the question.

    com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory
    com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit
        Nothing here JITs. Metal shaders are compiled to metallibs at
        build time and embedded in the binary.
  -->
</dict>
</plist>
